{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/60","id":4453355757,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSvcS2c8AAAABCXDQ7Q","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/60","diff_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/60.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/60.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/60","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/60/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/60/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/60/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/statuses/8b9e7477579d3f281b69b0f4137cb3319ae0dcb4","number":60,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Darwin: add source-bound R1 preview capabilities and manual upgrade","user":{"login":"pashamango","id":141678664,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHHYSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141678664?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Darwin's blanket listener prohibition cannot express a bounded preview deployment. This adds source-bound R1 capabilities for an installed static loopback preview broker and one additive tailnet-only Serve handler, while keeping the existing Codex command/sandbox defaults and all Wolfram runtime files unchanged.\n\nAuthority: Pasha's explicit local interactive `DARWIN-MAILBOX-0002-BOOTSTRAP-01` instruction. #57 is specification and #58 is diagnostic evidence (`POLICY_CONFLICT`); neither mailbox Issue authorizes changing its own dispatch protocol.\n\n## Behavior and boundaries\n\n- Strict JSON capability declarations inside one metadata block; only `loopback-user-service` and `tailscale-serve-additive`, R1, named application/port/operation/path. Unknown, duplicate, ambiguous, edited and unbound declarations fail closed. Capability-free tasks keep the restrictive command and infrastructure authority.\n- Worker only stages static content and an envelope-bound request. Installed code checks source, authoritative claim, outcome and protected runtime before applying the compiled loopback service/owned Serve operation. No arbitrary executable, LaunchAgent, listener, root/sudo, LAN/public bind, Funnel, SSH, ACL/key/auth changes, or generic infrastructure grant.\n- Creates/updates/removes owned static previews; Serve-only operations require an existing verified owned preview. Structural Serve comparisons preserve unrelated handlers. Existing Funnel or a dormant unowned route targeting the preview port blocks creation. Inverse operations and backups are retained; evidence accurately says `rollback-plan-verified`, not that a live rollback occurred.\n- Claims remain permanent; reporter/source/PR checks remain in force. #55/#56/#57/#58 are permanently ineligible in the new adapter. No historical Issue is edited, reset or replayed. No CEOffice deployment or live Darwin changes are included.\n- Ordinary tasks cannot authorize mailbox upgrades. Protected-file checks detect scope drift before completion; the documented residual same-UID boundary is not an OS isolation claim.\n\n## Validation\n\nTested head: `8b9e7477579d3f281b69b0f4137cb3319ae0dcb4`.\n\n`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: **108 tests PASS in 19.463 seconds**, including every original Wolfram/Darwin regression and new declaration, digest/envelope tamper, broker side-effect, failed mutation rollback, log-bound, installed-byte, upgrade recovery, watermark/history and offline smoke checks. `git diff --check` passes; working tree clean. Wolfram watcher/dispatcher/reporter/policy byte diff is empty.\n\nTests use fake Codex/GitHub/launchd/Tailscale and temporary installations. They are not live Darwin deployment evidence.\n\n## Manual merge and Darwin upgrade\n\nDo not auto-merge. Pasha must manually use **Create a merge commit**, so the tested head remains an ancestor of canonical main. Squash/rebase merges that discard it intentionally fail verification.\n\nAfter manual merge, run this **one exact command locally on Darwin** as the existing user:\n\n```sh\n(umask 077; upgrade_checkout=\"$(mktemp -d \"$HOME/ChitAkasha-Darwin/mailbox-upgrade-0002.XXXXXX\")\" && git clone --quiet --no-checkout https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab.git \"$upgrade_checkout\" && git -C \"$upgrade_checkout\" checkout --quiet --detach 8b9e7477579d3f281b69b0f4137cb3319ae0dcb4 && python3 \"$upgrade_checkout/tools/darwin-mailbox-upgrade\" upgrade --pr 60 --expected-head 8b9e7477579d3f281b69b0f4137cb3319ae0dcb4)\n```\n\nThe actual PR is **#60**; the tested head above is unchanged. A live read-only check of the merge verifier against open PR #60 rejects it before any installation operation.\n\nThe upgrader verifies actual PR number, trusted repository, exact branch/base/head, merged state, tested-head and merge ancestry, git/checkout/merged payload bytes, existing installed hashes and staged hashes before switching the runtime. It stages a whole release and atomically changes only the Darwin LaunchAgent pointer under install/cycle locks. A durable disable gate and recovery journal keep interrupted upgrades fail-closed. Original activation watermark, installation manifest, claims, runs, receipts and history are preserved. It never activates a new mailbox or creates a smoke Issue.\n\n## Harmless verification and rollback\n\nThe upgrade itself runs the verified installed offline smoke. Expect `legacy-restrictive: pass`, `capability-parsing-binding: pass`, `historical-execution-count: 0`, and `historical-state-unchanged: pass`. It checks legacy command/preamble, source parsing and envelope binding, permanent historical exclusions, and before/after history hashes without invoking queue dispatch, Codex, GitHub, launchd or Tailscale.\n\nTo repeat the harmless installed smoke after upgrade:\n\n```sh\npython3 -c 'import json,pathlib,subprocess,sys; b=pathlib.Path.home()/\"ChitAkasha-Darwin/agent-mailbox\"; j=json.loads((b/\"state/control/upgrade.json\").read_text()); subprocess.run([sys.executable,str(b/\"releases\"/j[\"merged\"]/\"tools/darwin-mailbox-upgrade\"),\"smoke\"],check=True)'\n```\n\nExact rollback command (also works when an interrupted upgrade left its journal/gate):\n\n```sh\npython3 -c 'import json,pathlib,subprocess,sys; b=pathlib.Path.home()/\"ChitAkasha-Darwin/agent-mailbox\"; j=json.loads((b/\"state/control/upgrade.json\").read_text()); subprocess.run([sys.executable,str(b/\"releases\"/j[\"merged\"]/\"tools/darwin-mailbox-upgrade\"),\"rollback\"],check=True)'\n```\n\nRollback uses the verified upgraded release's `tools/darwin-mailbox-upgrade rollback`: verifies the old installed bytes, restores only the old Darwin LaunchAgent pointer, and preserves even new claims accumulated since upgrade. Recovery after interruption uses the same command and leaves polling disabled if validation/restart fails. Separate preview-task deployments are not silently undone by a mailbox rollback.\n\nDetailed contract, limitations and recovery: [docs/darwin-mailbox-capabilities.md](https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/blob/8b9e7477579d3f281b69b0f4137cb3319ae0dcb4/docs/darwin-mailbox-capabilities.md).\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T22:38:42Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T22:49:17Z","closed_at":"2026-09-05T22:49:17Z","merged_at":"2026-09-05T22:49:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"530c1ac968718cc2ef501f5620537108f61f11b2","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"pashamango:agent/wolfram/DARWIN-MAILBOX-0002-BOOTSTRAP-01","ref":"agent/wolfram/DARWIN-MAILBOX-0002-BOOTSTRAP-01","repo":{"id":1257706201,"node_id":"R_kgDOSvcS2Q","name":"minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab","full_name":"pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab","owner":{"login":"pashamango","id":141678664,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHHYSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141678664?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":true,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Private lab for Minutta RP/PR cycle rehearsal","homepage":null,"language":"Python